<title>USA: U.S. FTC cautious on electronic money regulation.</title>
<headline>U.S. FTC cautious on electronic money regulation.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of the U.S. Federal Trade Commission Thursday backed a cautious approach to regulation of electronic money.</p>
<p>&quot;I suspect it makes sense to err on the side of under- rather than over-regulation,&quot; FTC Chairman Robert Pitofsky told a Treasury conference on electronic money.</p>
<p>&quot;Market-created solutions, voluntary self-regulation and technological fixes may do the trick,&quot; he said. &quot;If and when private solutions prove inadequate, government must be ready to step in,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
